<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαπάζω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		 and Lyr. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαπάω,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>; 
			Dor.
		3pl.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-οντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					4(5).54
				</span></i>
			; 
				Ep.
			
			impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγάπαζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1291
				</span></i>
			:—also in 
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>; 
				Dor.
			
			impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ̄γαπάζοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.241
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Diotog.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.7.62
			</span></i>:— only in pres. and impf.,
			exc. aor. act. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαπάξαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Callicrat.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.28.18
			</span></i>:—<i>treat with affection, receive with outward
				signs of love,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δὲ πατὴρ ὃν παῖδα . . ἀγαπάζει,
					ἐλθόντ᾽ ἐξ ἀπίης γαίης δεκάτῳ ἐνιαυτῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεμεσσητὸν δέ κεν εἴη ἀθάνατον θεὸν
					ὧδε βροτοὺς ἀγαπαζέμεν ἄντην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.464
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1327
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			 in abs. sense, <i>show signs of love, caress,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνεον ἀγαπαζόμενοι κεφαλήν τε καὶ
					ὤμους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.224
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., like
			
				Act.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
			</span></i>l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ δώροις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.416
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>welcome, receive gratefully,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμαὶ καλλίνικον χάρμ᾽ ἀγαπάζοντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
				</span></i>
			 l.c.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
